WEBVTT

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:15.816
Hi, I’m Muhammad Husain Aboutalebi, an AI, mechanical, and software engineer.

00:00:15.816 --> 00:00:22.883
Welcome to Sentix, an enterprise-grade Predictive Maintenance platform that I engineered from the ground up.

00:00:22.883 --> 00:00:27.283
I start by orchestrating the microservices using Docker Compose.

00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:32.916
I configured this setup to provision a fully localized, air-gapped environment—ensuring secure,

00:00:32.916 --> 00:00:41.316
resilient, and deterministic deployments across the backend, Redis, frontend, and AI services.

00:00:41.316 --> 00:00:44.766
Here in Portainer, I'll show you the FastAPI service logs.

00:00:44.766 --> 00:00:51.800
What you are seeing is a real-time, physics-based mathematical simulation of rotary machinery that I modeled and implemented.

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:55.316
By generating high-frequency thermal and tri-axial vibration telemetry,

00:00:55.316 --> 00:01:00.616
my engine accurately simulates mechanical degradation and fault dynamics right at the edge.

00:01:00.616 --> 00:01:05.366
Next, I’ll demonstrate the AI diagnostic engine via the API documentation.

00:01:05.366 --> 00:01:13.100
I designed and built an offline Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipeline powered by a localized Llama 3.2 model and FAISS

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:19.716
vector indexing. When querying OEM equipment manuals, my engine doesn't just generate troubleshooting steps—it extracts and

00:01:19.716 --> 00:01:26.216
cites exact source pages. This provides field technicians with instant, auditable standard operating

00:01:26.216 --> 00:01:29.100
procedures with zero external cloud dependency.

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:36.216
Finally, let's look at the ingestion layer in RedisInsight. To handle industrial-scale throughput without database bottlenecks, I

00:01:36.216 --> 00:01:43.300
architected the streaming pipeline around Redis Streams for sub-millisecond processing. I also engineered an in-memory

00:01:43.300 --> 00:01:49.450
deduplication and state verification mechanism that captures mechanical anomalies in real time, eliminating

00:01:49.450 --> 00:01:54.216
alert fatigue while ensuring critical failure states are logged instantly.

00:01:54.216 --> 00:02:01.516
This project represents my end-to-end execution at the intersection of mechanical engineering and modern scalable software architecture.

00:02:01.516 --> 00:02:02.483
Thanks for watching!